H("735.d.5.H",3,"Presenting the portfolio to a panel of professionals calls for:","formal presentation skills",["casual chatting only","reading silently","avoiding questions"],"Panels expect polished delivery.")
H("735.d.5.H",4,"A strong formal presentation includes a clear introduction, organized content and:","a response to the panel's questions",["a rush to finish","a silent exit","a joke only"],"Handling questions shows mastery.")
H("735.d.6.A",3,"A student collects transcripts, volunteer hours, certificates and work experience into one folder for job applications. This is:","creating a portfolio documenting accomplishments",["deleting records","hiding records","losing records"],"Portfolios gather proof of accomplishments.")
H("735.d.6.A",4,"A career portfolio should include evidence of:","academics, volunteer work, employment and certifications",["only game scores","only social posts","only passwords"],"Breadth shows readiness.")
H("735.d.6.B",3,"A student puts the most relevant projects first and groups related items together. This is:","organizing and prioritizing portfolio information",["scrambling it","hiding it","deleting it"],"Organization helps reviewers.")
H("735.d.6.B",4,"Which approach best prioritizes portfolio content for a cybersecurity job?","Put security projects and certifications first",["Put unrelated photos first","Put hobbies first","Hide the projects"],"Relevance guides priority.")
H("735.d.6.C",3,"A portfolio cover letter, a slide deck and a short demo video show:","written, verbal and visual communication",["only one type of communication","no communication","only voice"],"Portfolios use all three forms.")
H("735.d.6.C",4,"Industry-standard communication in a portfolio means writing that is:","clear, professional and organized",["sloppy","slang-heavy","unreadable"],"Standards demand professionalism.")

# ---- 736 IT Practicum II / Advanced ----
