H("737.d.6.F",3,"A student questions assumptions, tests the fix and checks the data before accepting it. This is:","critical-thinking analysis and evaluation of a solution",["accepting without proof","copying","avoiding checks"],"Evaluation uses evidence.")
H("737.d.6.F",4,"Evaluating a proposed technological solution critically means asking:","does the evidence show it works and what could go wrong?",["is it popular?","is it expensive?","is it colorful?"],"Critical evaluation looks at evidence and risk.")
H("737.d.6.G",3,"A sustainability plan for a computer lab fix describes how the solution will be:","maintained and supported over time",["forgotten","hidden","abandoned"],"Sustainability keeps solutions working.")
H("737.d.6.G",4,"Part of a sustainability plan for a replacement PC program is:","scheduling updates and replacement cycles",["ignoring updates","avoiding budgets","removing support"],"Planning replacements sustains service.")
H("737.d.6.H",3,"A student uses a simulator, a spreadsheet and a manual to design and test a network change. This is:","selecting and using appropriate technological resources",["random tools","avoiding tools","one tool only"],"Right tools support research and design.")
H("737.d.6.H",4,"Choosing technological resources for research and design should be based on:","how well they fit the task",["which is newest","which is largest","which is cheapest only"],"Fit to task matters.")
H("737.d.6.I",3,"Notes, drafts, test logs and diagrams kept throughout a project make up its:","documentation of the research and development process",["trash","final exam","budget"],"Documentation records the process.")
H("737.d.6.I",4,"Good R&D documentation should be:","dated, organized and detailed enough for others to follow",["vague","unordered","hidden"],"Clear records are useful.")
H("737.d.6.J",3,"At the end of the project, the student presents the solution to a panel of professionals using:","formal presentation skills",["casual chat","silence","reading from notes without looking up"],"Panels expect polish.")
H("737.d.6.J",4,"A professional presentation of a solution to a panel includes:","a clear problem, the solution, evidence and answers to questions",["only the title","only a joke","a hurried exit"],"Complete presentations are persuasive.")
H("737.d.7.A",3,"A project begins with initiating and planning, then executing, monitoring and controlling, and finally closing. These are:","project methodology phases",["hardware parts","file types","network cables"],"Project management follows phases.")
H("737.d.7.A",4,"In the monitoring and controlling phase, the project manager:","tracks progress and makes corrections",["ends the project","starts the plan","ignores issues"],"Monitoring keeps projects on track.")
H("737.d.7.B",3,"The scope of work statement for a lab upgrade lists:","what will and won't be included in the project",["only the budget","only lunch plans","nothing"],"Scope sets boundaries.")
H("737.d.7.B",4,"Defining scope helps a team avoid:","scope creep, where extra work keeps being added",["all deadlines","all costs","all risks"],"Clear scope controls growth.")
H("737.d.7.C",3,"A project plan lists each task, who does it and when it is due. This is a:","time and activity plan",["recipe","logo","slogan"],"Activity plans schedule tasks.")
H("737.d.7.C",4,"Which tool is commonly used to show task schedules over time?","a Gantt chart",["a pie chart only","a flowchart only","a bar code"],"Gantt charts show schedules.")
H("737.d.7.D",3,"A project team includes a network engineer, a developer and a trainer who each handle their own area. This is a:","cross-functional team",["single-skill team","random group","one-person team"],"Cross-functional teams combine skills.")
H("737.d.7.D",4,"The advantage of a cross-functional team is that it:","brings different expertise to reach project goals",["avoids communication","limits skills","duplicates work"],"Diverse skills solve complex projects.")
H("737.d.7.E",3,"A QA test plan lists test cases, expected results and who runs them. This ensures:","the product meets requirements before release",["it is never tested","bugs stay hidden","deadlines vanish"],"Test plans verify quality.")
H("737.d.7.E",4,"A quality assurance test plan should include:","test cases, pass/fail criteria and a way to log defects",["only the title","no steps","only opinions"],"Good plans are specific.")
H("737.d.7.F",3,"A contingency plan describes what to do if:","something goes wrong with the project",["everything goes right","no one works","the budget is perfect"],"Contingency plans prepare for problems.")
H("737.d.7.F",4,"A contingency plan for a server migration should include:","a rollback procedure and backup contacts",["no backups","no contacts","random steps"],"Fallback plans reduce risk.")
H("737.d.8.A",3,"Viruses, ransomware and phishing are examples of:","security threats to information systems",["office supplies","software upgrades","display types"],"Threats target systems.")
H("737.d.8.A",4,"A threat that locks files until money is paid is called:","ransomware",["firmware","bandwidth","a driver"],"Ransomware encrypts files for ransom.")
H("737.d.8.B",3,"A security lapse, such as an unpatched server, can lead to:","data breaches and loss of trust",["faster networks","free upgrades","higher grades"],"Lapses create vulnerabilities.")
H("737.d.8.B",4,"Identifying security needs means deciding what must be protected, such as:","customer data, system access and equipment",["only paper","only furniture","nothing"],"Assets drive security needs.")
H("737.d.8.C",3,"After finding that employees reuse weak passwords, a team writes a plan with password rules and training. This is:","developing and implementing a plan to address a threat",["ignoring the threat","blaming users","deleting accounts"],"Plans address identified risks.")
H("737.d.8.C",4,"An effective security plan includes controls, responsibilities and:","a way to monitor whether the controls work",["no monitoring","no owners","no review"],"Monitoring verifies controls.")
H("737.d.8.D",3,"Writing down the steps for revoking a departed employee's access is:","documenting security procedures",["wasting time","hiding information","deleting steps"],"Documented procedures ensure consistency.")
H("737.d.8.D",4,"Documented security procedures help organizations because they:","make responses consistent and auditable",["slow everything","remove accountability","hide mistakes"],"Procedures create consistency.")
H("737.d.8.E",3,"Investigators examining a hacked computer to find evidence are using:","computer forensics",["interior design","cooking","gardening"],"Forensics gathers digital evidence.")
H("737.d.8.E",4,"A key rule in computer forensics is to:","preserve the original evidence and work from copies",["alter the original","delete logs","share evidence publicly"],"Evidence integrity matters.")
H("737.d.9.A",3,"A technician lets a client explain a problem without interrupting and takes notes. This is:","effective listening to identify support needs",["ignoring the client","rushing","guessing"],"Listening reveals needs.")
H("737.d.9.A",4,"To confirm understanding of a client's request, a technician should:","restate it in their own words and ask if it's right",["assume correctness","avoid questions","end the call"],"Paraphrasing confirms understanding.")
H("737.d.9.B",3,"After listening, a technician lists the client's needs and outlines steps and timeframes. This is:","identifying customer need and formulating a support plan",["canceling service","avoiding work","guessing"],"Needs drive support plans.")
H("737.d.9.B",4,"A support plan should include:","the goal, the steps, the responsible person and the timeline",["no steps","no goal","no owner"],"Plans are actionable.")
H("737.d.9.C",3,"A technician runs a report of all computers with outdated software and checks system information. This is:","creating queries and reports to assess system information",["avoiding data","guessing","deleting logs"],"Queries and reports reveal conditions.")
H("737.d.9.C",4,"A query that lists only machines with less than 10% free disk space helps the technician to:","find systems that need attention first",["delete the machines","rename the machines","ignore the machines"],"Targeted queries prioritize work.")
H("737.d.9.D",3,"A technician uses a step-by-step method to find why a laptop won't charge and then fixes it. This is:","problem-solving in support, maintenance and repair",["guessing","blaming","avoiding"],"Methodical problem solving fixes issues.")
H("737.d.9.D",4,"The first step in solving a repair problem is usually to:","define the problem and gather information",["replace parts at random","give up","skip diagnosis"],"Diagnosis precedes repair.")
H("737.d.9.E",3,"A program that tests memory and a tool that checks hard drive health are examples of:","hardware and software diagnostics",["wallpapers","games","fonts"],"Diagnostics find faults.")
H("737.d.9.E",4,"Running a diagnostic before replacing a part helps avoid:","unnecessary repairs and costs",["all testing","all learning","all support"],"Diagnose first.")
H("737.d.9.F",3,"After fixing a problem, the technician tells the user what caused it and what was done. This is:","reporting the cause and solution to the user",["hiding the cause","ignoring the user","blaming the user"],"Users should know the result.")
H("737.d.9.F",4,"When reporting a solution to a non-technical user, the technician should:","explain in plain language and offer prevention tips",["use heavy jargon","skip details","blame them"],"Clear explanations build trust.")
H("737.d.9.G",3,"A ticket note lists the symptom, cause and fix so others can use it later. This is:","written documentation of the problem and its solution",["a disposable note","an error","a delay"],"Documentation preserves knowledge.")
H("737.d.9.G",4,"Documentation of a repair should be:","clear, accurate and stored where others can find it",["vague","hidden","incomplete"],"Findable records help the team.")
H("737.d.10.A",3,"A technician installs an antivirus program on a new workstation. This is:","installing security software",["deleting software","hiding software","removing protection"],"Security software protects systems.")
H("737.d.10.A",4,"Before installing security software, a technician should confirm that:","it is from a trusted source and compatible with the system",["it is free of any license","it is unknown","it is old"],"Verify source and compatibility.")
H("737.d.10.B",3,"Antivirus definitions must be updated regularly so the software can:","detect the newest threats",["use less power","print faster","look better"],"Definitions identify known malware.")
H("737.d.10.B",4,"Setting security software to update automatically ensures that it:","stays current without relying on users",["stops working","needs no testing","blocks all files"],"Automatic updates keep protection fresh.")
H("737.d.10.C",3,"A technician boots an infected computer into safe mode and runs a full scan to remove malware. This is:","using security software to clean an infected machine",["spreading the malware","ignoring the issue","deleting the OS"],"Scans remove threats.")
H("737.d.10.C",4,"After cleaning an infected machine, the technician should:","re-scan, apply updates and change passwords as needed",["assume it's clean","reinstall the malware","share the infection"],"Verification and hardening finish the job.")
H("737.d.11.A",3,"A written disaster recovery plan explains how to:","restore systems and data after a major failure",["avoid backups","ignore outages","delete systems"],"DR plans restore operations.")
H("737.d.11.A",4,"A disaster recovery plan should list:","critical systems, backup locations and recovery steps",["only lunch menus","only passwords","random notes"],"Specifics enable recovery.")
H("737.d.11.B",3,"A written preventive maintenance plan schedules tasks such as:","cleaning fans, checking cables and applying updates",["ignoring equipment","waiting for failure","deleting logs"],"Preventive maintenance reduces failures.")
H("737.d.11.B",4,"A preventive maintenance schedule helps an IT department by:","reducing unexpected failures and downtime",["increasing failures","ending support","removing documentation"],"Regular upkeep prevents problems.")
H("737.d.12.A",3,"A student collects project reports, certifications and volunteer records into a career portfolio. This is:","documenting projects and accomplishments",["deleting work","hiding work","losing work"],"Portfolios show achievements.")
H("737.d.12.A",4,"A portfolio documents academics, volunteer experience and:","employment and certifications",["only pets","only recipes","only games"],"Breadth shows readiness.")
H("737.d.12.B",3,"A student places the best, most relevant items at the front of the portfolio. This is:","organizing and prioritizing information",["scrambling it","hiding it","deleting it"],"Prioritizing guides reviewers.")
H("737.d.12.B",4,"The best way to organize a portfolio for a hiring manager is by:","relevance to the job and clear sections",["random order","alphabet only","file size"],"Relevance and structure help readers.")
H("737.d.12.C",3,"A portfolio's cover letter, slide show and oral presentation show:","written, verbal and visual communication skills",["no skills","one skill","only typing"],"Portfolios demonstrate communication.")
H("737.d.12.C",4,"Communication in a portfolio should be consistent with:","IT industry standards for clarity and professionalism",["slang","no rules","random style"],"Industry standards guide quality.")

# ---- 738 IT Advanced Practicum ----
H("738.d.1.A",3,"In an advanced practicum, a student drafts a project memo, gives a verbal update to a client and shares a system diagram. This uses:","written, verbal and visual communication consistent with IT standards",["one type of communication","no communication","only email"],"Practicum communication blends forms.")
H("738.d.1.A",4,"Which communication practice meets IT industry standards?","Documenting decisions in a clear, dated written record",["Relying on memory only","Using unexplained slang","Skipping written updates"],"Standards favor clear records.")
H("738.d.1.B",3,"A technician reads log data, summarizes the likely cause and explains it to a manager. This is:","analyzing, interpreting and communicating information",["hiding information","guessing","ignoring data"],"Analysis plus communication drives action.")
H("738.d.1.B",4,"To effectively communicate technical findings to a non-technical audience, a technician should:","translate details into plain language and focus on impact",["use the most jargon possible","read raw logs aloud","avoid questions"],"Audience-aware communication works best.")
H("738.d.1.C",3,"A technician pauses, nods and asks a clarifying question when a client describes an error. This is:","active listening to obtain and clarify information",["interrupting","multitasking","ignoring"],"Active listening obtains accurate details.")
H("738.d.1.C",4,"Which question helps clarify a vague client report like 'the network is down'?","Which devices or locations are affected and since when?",["Why are you bothering me?","Did you try turning off the building?","Is it Friday?"],"Specific questions reduce ambiguity.")
H("738.d.1.D",3,"A technician follows up after a fix to be sure the client is satisfied. This is:","public relations skills that maintain customer satisfaction",["ignoring the customer","avoiding contact","hiding results"],"Follow-up builds relationships.")
H("738.d.1.D",4,"Keeping internal clients, such as accounting, satisfied with IT service includes:","meeting commitments and communicating delays early",["avoiding updates","blaming them","delaying replies"],"Reliability and transparency maintain trust.")
H("738.d.2",3,"A student faces a complex outage, examines possible causes, tests solutions and selects the best fix, working alone and with a team. This reflects:","advanced problem-solving using critical thinking and decision making",["random guessing","avoiding the problem","copying the fix"],"Advanced problem solving combines analysis and decisions.")
H("738.d.2",4,"A student demonstrating advanced problem-solving with increased fluency will:","evaluate alternatives and justify a technology-based decision",["pick the first idea","avoid data","rely on luck"],"Justified decisions show advanced skill.")
H("738.d.3.A",3,"A student follows the lab's rules for passwords, visitor logs and equipment checkout every day. This is:","understanding and consistently following IT security rules",["ignoring rules","sharing logins","skipping logs"],"Consistency is key to security.")
H("738.d.3.A",4,"Following IT security procedures consistently reduces the risk of:","breaches caused by human error",["faster networks","free equipment","higher grades"],"Procedures limit mistakes.")
H("738.d.3.B",3,"A technician sees repeated failed logins from an unknown address, blocks it and updates the firewall software. This is:","recognizing a threat and addressing it with security software",["ignoring the alert","deleting logs","sharing the address"],"Detect and respond.")
H("738.d.3.B",4,"After recognizing a threat, a technician should install updates and:","verify the protection is working",["assume it works","disable it","ignore logs"],"Verification closes the loop.")
H("738.d.3.C",3,"A student explains that an unpatched server could expose customer records. This is:","identifying security needs and the problems lapses cause",["ignoring risk","avoiding review","hiding records"],"Understanding consequences guides security.")
H("738.d.3.C",4,"With increased proficiency, a technician can predict which security lapse would cause the greatest harm and:","prioritize protections for those systems first",["ignore it","treat all risks the same","avoid planning"],"Risk-based prioritization.")
H("738.d.3.D",3,"Before using a power drill to install a rack, a technician should:","wear safety glasses and check the tool",["skip safety","use bare hands","use a broken tool"],"Safe tool use protects people.")
H("738.d.3.D",4,"With increased proficiency in computer technology safety, a technician will:","use tools correctly without being reminded",["need constant reminders","avoid safety","skip checks"],"Proficiency shows in habits.")
H("738.d.3.E",3,"Used toner cartridges and batteries are handled as hazardous materials and should be:","disposed of through approved recycling programs",["thrown in regular trash","burned","buried"],"Hazardous materials need proper disposal.")
H("738.d.3.E",4,"Proper disposal of environmentally hazardous IT materials protects:","people and the environment from harmful substances",["only the budget","only the building","no one"],"Disposal laws protect health.")
H("738.d.4.A",3,"A student completes assigned tasks on time and with care without being reminded. This shows:","a positive, productive work ethic",["a poor attitude","avoidance","neglect"],"Reliability reflects work ethic.")
H("738.d.4.A",4,"Performing tasks as directed in a practicum includes:","following instructions and asking questions when unsure",["ignoring instructions","guessing","avoiding feedback"],"Following directions and seeking clarity is professional.")
H("738.d.4.B",3,"An IT employee refuses to read a coworker's private email even though they have admin access. This is:","practicing ethical responsibilities in IT",["breaking rules","spying","ignoring ethics"],"Access doesn't mean permission.")
H("738.d.4.B",4,"Which is a legal responsibility in the field of IT?","complying with software licensing and data protection laws",["ignoring licenses","selling user data","copying software freely"],"IT workers must follow laws.")
H("738.d.4.C",3,"A technician admits to a mistake that caused a short outage rather than hiding it. This shows:","integrity by choosing the ethical course",["dishonesty","avoidance","blame shifting"],"Integrity means honesty.")
H("738.d.4.C",4,"When a manager asks for a shortcut that violates policy, a person with integrity will:","explain the policy and follow the rules",["break the policy","hide the issue","blame a coworker"],"Ethics outweigh convenience.")
H("738.d.4.D",3,"A student complies with the school's acceptable-use policy and copyright law at all times. This is:","complying with all applicable rules, laws and regulations consistently",["breaking rules sometimes","ignoring laws","hiding violations"],"Consistent compliance is professional.")
H("738.d.4.D",4,"Consistent compliance with regulations in IT matters because noncompliance can result in:","fines, legal action and loss of trust",["higher pay","new equipment","faster networks"],"Noncompliance has consequences.")
H("738.d.5.A",3,"A student chooses a ticketing system to track tasks, a wiki to document and a spreadsheet to evaluate results. This is:","selecting and using appropriate technological resources",["random tools","one tool only","no tools"],"Right tools support learning activities.")
H("738.d.5.A",4,"A technological resource should be selected based on whether it:","fits the task and supports documentation and evaluation",["is newest","is largest","looks best"],"Fit to task matters.")
H("738.d.5.B",3,"A technician reads a rack diagram and wiring schematic to plan a cabling job. This is:","reading and interpreting technical documentation",["guessing","ignoring diagrams","skipping plans"],"Diagrams guide installations.")
H("738.d.5.B",4,"Which document would best show how network devices are physically connected?","a network diagram",["a menu","a poster","a calendar"],"Diagrams show topology.")
H("738.d.5.C",3,"A technician uses vendor manuals, forums and search engines fluently to resolve an unfamiliar error. This is:","employing reference tools and Internet sources with fluency",["avoiding information","guessing","ignoring the error"],"Fluent research solves problems.")
H("738.d.5.C",4,"A technician evaluating information from a forum should:","verify it against official documentation before applying it",["trust it automatically","ignore all sources","apply it blindly"],"Verify unverified advice.")
H("738.d.5.D",3,"A student designs a backup strategy using industry-standard practices and appropriate tools. This is:","developing a solution using technologies, IT concepts and standards",["avoiding standards","guessing","copying"],"Solutions follow standards.")
H("738.d.5.D",4,"Developing solutions with increased proficiency means the student can:","design, test and justify solutions that meet standards",["need constant help","avoid testing","ignore standards"],"Proficiency shows independence.")
H("738.d.5.E",3,"A student uses scope, schedule and quality checkpoints to manage an information system upgrade. This is:","implementing project methodologies to manage projects",["avoiding planning","working randomly","skipping steps"],"Methodologies guide projects.")
H("738.d.5.E",4,"A project methodology for an information system project typically moves from planning to:","execution, monitoring and closing",["deletion","confusion","random work"],"Phases structure the project.")
H("738.d.5.F",3,"A student saves a finished design document, a test report and a client letter as proof of their practicum work. These are:","representative work samples",["unrelated files","drafts only","blank pages"],"Samples demonstrate skills.")
H("738.d.5.F",4,"Representative work samples should be:","relevant, high quality and clearly labeled",["random","unfinished","unlabeled"],"Good samples are curated.")

B.balance()
B.save(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "..", "batches", "cte_92.jsonl"))
